{"type":"message","id":"06d029a7","parentId":"755ab7db","timestamp":"2026-08-01T07:36:57.044Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, adding `tap 'homebrew/cask-versions'` to your Brewfile can be useful if you want to install alternative versions of cask applications (e.g., older or beta versions of apps like Firefox, Chrome, or VS Code). The `homebrew/cask-versions` tap provides access to these alternative versions.\n\n### Steps to Add the Tap:\n1. Open your `Brewfile`.\n2. Add the following line:\n   ```ruby\n   tap 'homebrew/cask-versions'\n   ```\n3. Run `brew bundle dump` to update the Brewfile with the tap.\n4. Run `brew bundle install` to apply the changes.\n\n### Example Use Case:\nIf you want to install Firefox Developer Edition alongside the stable version, you can add:\n```ruby\ncask 'firefox-developer-edition'\n```\n\n### Verification:\n- Check if the tap is already installed:\n  ```bash\n  brew tap | grep cask-versions\n  ```\n- If not, manually tap it:\n  ```bash\n  brew tap homebrew/cask-versions\n  ```\n\nWould you like me to add this tap to your Brewfile now?"}],"api":"mistral-conversations","provider":"mistral","model":"devstral-medium-latest","usage":{"input":2808,"output":242,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":3050,"cost":{"input":0.0011232000000000002,"output":0.000484,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0016072000000000003}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1785569804445,"responseId":"1e0f71bea80d4b2abc713da455fc9da0","rawStopReason":"stop"}}
